---
/*
 * /learn/ai-receptionist-cost — cost-query page with real numbers, the
 * pricing data AI agents and owners both look for.
 */
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import SiteNav from "../../components/SiteNav.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../../components/SiteFooter.astro";

const title = "How Much Does an AI Receptionist Cost in 2026? | Arkansas Automated";
const description =
  "Real AI receptionist pricing: $2,500 setup plus $497 a month with Arkansas Automated, versus $2,500 to $3,500 a month for a hire and $1 to $2 a minute for answering services.";

const site = "https://arkansasautomated.com";
const pageUrl = `${site}/learn/ai-receptionist-cost`;
const schema = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "Article",
      headline: "How Much Does an AI Receptionist Cost in 2026?",
      description,
      author: { "@type": "Person", name: "Andre Brassfield", jobTitle: "Founder, Arkansas Automated" },
      publisher: { "@type": "Organization", name: "Arkansas Automated", url: site },
      datePublished: "2026-07-29",
      dateModified: "2026-08-07",
      mainEntityOfPage: pageUrl,
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      itemListElement: [
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 1, name: "Home", item: `${site}/` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 2, name: "Learn", item: `${site}/learn` },
        { "@type": "ListItem", position: 3, name: "AI receptionist cost", item: pageUrl },
      ],
    },
  ],
};
---

<Base title={title} description={description} path="/learn/ai-receptionist-cost" schema={schema} ogType="article">
  <SiteNav />
  <main>
    <article class="hero">
      <div class="container">
        <nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb">
          <a href="/">Home</a><span>/</span><a href="/learn">Learn</a><span>/</span>AI receptionist cost
        </nav>
        <h1 class="heading-xl measure">What an AI receptionist costs.</h1>
        <p class="body-lg measure" style="margin-top:1.15rem">
          With Arkansas Automated, an AI receptionist costs $2,500 to set up and $497 a month,
          flat. A full-time human receptionist in Arkansas costs $2,500 to $3,500 a month before
          payroll tax and covers a quarter of the week. A per-minute answering service costs
          $1 to $2 per minute, which quietly becomes $800 to $2,000 a month at real call volume.
        </p>
        <p class="fine-print" style="margin-top:1.5rem">
          Last updated August 7, 2026. Written by Andre Brassfield, founder of Arkansas Automated.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <section class="section section-tint">
      <div class="container article-body">
        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">The three ways businesses cover the phone</h2>

        <div class="table-wrap" style="margin:1.5rem 0 0.5rem">
          <table class="compare-table">
            <caption style="text-align:left;padding:0 0 1rem;color:var(--text-secondary);font-size:.95rem">
              Dated pricing, as of August 7, 2026.
            </caption>
            <thead>
              <tr>
                <th></th>
                <th>AI front desk (Arkansas Automated)</th>
                <th>Human receptionist</th>
                <th>Per-minute answering service</th>
              </tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Setup</th>
                <td>$2,500 flat</td>
                <td>Hiring, training, and turnover</td>
                <td>None</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Monthly cost</th>
                <td>$497 flat</td>
                <td>$2,500 to $3,500 before payroll tax</td>
                <td>$800 to $2,000 at 300 short calls</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Coverage</th>
                <td>24/7, nights and weekends</td>
                <td>Roughly 40 of the week's 168 hours</td>
                <td>24/7</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">Billing</th>
                <td>Flat, no per-minute meter</td>
                <td>Salary plus tax and benefits</td>
                <td>$1 to $2 per minute</td>
              </tr>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row">What it does</th>
                <td>Answers, qualifies, and books onto your calendar</td>
                <td>Answers and handles judgment calls</td>
                <td>Answers and takes a message</td>
              </tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="fine-print" style="margin-bottom:2rem">
          All figures in USD. See the full price sheet at
          <a class="text-link" href="/services">services and pricing</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">What each option is really paying for</h2>
        <p>
          <strong>Hire a receptionist.</strong> $30,000 to $42,000 a year fully loaded in
          Arkansas, covering 40 of the week's 168 hours, before turnover, training, and sick
          days. The right answer at real scale, and the wrong one for a shop where the owner
          still answers between jobs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>Per-minute answering service.</strong> $1 to $2 per minute sounds cheap until
          you do the multiplication. A service business fielding 300 short calls a month at two
          to three minutes each is spending $800 to $2,000 monthly, and the operators still
          take messages instead of booking jobs.
        </p>
        <p>
          <strong>AI front desk.</strong> $2,500 setup plus $497 a month with us, flat, no
          per-minute meter. Call volume, nights, weekends, and storm surges included. Monthly
          tuning with a human included. That is the number on our website because we think you
          should be able to read it without a sales call.
        </p>

        <h2 class="heading-lg measure">What the $497 a month has to beat</h2>
        <p>
          For most Arkansas service businesses the break-even is one or two jobs a month. An
          HVAC replacement, a roof, a new dental family, a retained legal client: any one of
          those pays for months of service. The missed call is never a line item on the P&L,
          which is exactly why it leaks for years.
        </p>
        <p>
          If your call volume is genuinely low, we will tell you on the assessment call and
          point you at the cheaper fix. The $999 operations audit exists for businesses that
          want the math in writing before committing to anything.
        </p>

        <div class="next-step">
          <p>
            See the full price sheet at <a class="text-link" href="/services">services and
            pricing</a>, or <a class="text-link" href="/#reserve">book the free assessment</a>
            and hear the receptionist answer as your business.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="link-chips" style="margin-top:2.5rem">
          <a class="chip" href="/learn/what-is-an-ai-receptionist">What is an AI receptionist?</a>
          <a class="chip" href="/learn/ai-receptionist-vs-answering-service">AI vs answering service</a>
          <a class="chip chip-strong" href="/learn">All guides</a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
  <SiteFooter />
</Base>
